1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,600
When they buried Margorie McCall, an
expensive ring was still on her finger.

2
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:08,760
Her husband had tried to take it off, but
her finger was too swollen.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:11,207
Margorie had died of a fever,

4
00:00:11,207 --> 00:00:14,900
and her family rushed the burial, afraid
the illness might spread.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,020
That very night, while the

6
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:20,660
earth on her grave was still loose,
thieves came to the graveyard.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,480
They knew about the ring.

8
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:26,480
They opened the coffin and tried to pull
it off, but it wouldn't budge.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,800
So one of them pulled out a knife:

10
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:32,160
if he couldn't remove the ring, he would
cut off her finger.

11
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,220
The blade touched her skin.

12
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:36,540
And at that very moment, the

13
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:40,220
woman they believed was dead sat up in the
coffin and screamed.

14
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:42,700
The thieves ran for their lives,

15
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:46,540
while Margorie climbed out of the grave
and walked home in her burial clothes.

16
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:50,360
Her husband was sitting with their
children when someone knocked at the door.

17
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:52,720
He froze and said, “ If

18
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:56,040
your mother were still alive, I'd swear
that was her knock.”

19
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:57,540
He opened the door.

20
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:02,900
There stood Margorie, in the clothes she'd
been buried in, with blood on her hand.

21
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:07,220
When he saw his wife, he clutched his
chest and dropped dead.

22
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:12,240
A few days later, they buried him in the
very coffin Margorie had climbed out of.

23
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:16,800
She lived for many more years, married
again, and had children.

24
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:21,120
And when her own time came, these words
were carved on her headstone:  “

25
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:24,000
Lived once, buried twice.”
